<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&#160;</p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">The Company&#8217;s accounts receivable primarily
includes balances due from customers when the Company&#8217;s wheelchair and living aids products have been sold and delivered to customers,
the Company&#8217;s contracted performance obligations have been satisfied, amount billed and the Company has an unconditional right
to payment, which has not been collected as of the balance sheet dates.</p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">For accounts receivable, approximately <ix:nonFraction contextRef="c0" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="zjyl:AccountsReceivablePercentage" scale="-2" unitRef="pure" id="ixv-25233">47.8</ix:nonFraction>%,
or $<ix:nonFraction contextRef="c2" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LongTermAccountsNotesAndLoansReceivableNetNoncurrent" scale="6" unitRef="usd" id="ixv-25234">2.8</ix:nonFraction> million of the September 30, 2025 balance have been subsequently collected. The remaining balance of approximately $<ix:nonFraction contextRef="c122" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LongTermAccountsNotesAndLoansReceivableNetNoncurrent" scale="6" unitRef="usd" id="ixv-25235">3.0</ix:nonFraction> million
is expected to be collected before September 30, 2026.</p></ix:nonNumeric><div>
